.\nSo team B scores 4 * 2 = 8 goals in the second half.\nThe total number of goals scored by team A is 4 + 1 = 5.\nThe total number of goals scored by team B is 2 + 8 = 10.\nThe total number of goals scored in the match is 5 + 10 = 15.\nThe answer is 15.\n\nAnswer_15:\nThe teacher uses 20% of the chalk each day.\nHe uses 45% of the chalk on Monday.\nSo he uses 45 / 20 = 2.25 days worth of chalk.\nThe answer is 2.25.\n\nAnswer_16:\nThere are 12 boys and 12 girls.\nOne-third of the girls are on varsity.\nSo 12 / 3 = 4 girls are on varsity.\nOne-fourth of the boys are on varsity.\nSo 12 / 4 = 3 boys are on varsity.\nThe total number of students on varsity is 4 + 3 = 7.\nThe total number of students is 12 + 12 = 24.\nThe number of students not on varsity is 24 - 7 = 17.\nThe answer is 17.\n\nAnswer_17:\nMike buys 5 face masks.\nJohnny buys 2 more than thrice as many as Mike.\nSo Johnny buys 2 + 3 * 5 = 17 face masks.\nThe answer is 17.\n\nAnswer_18:\nJames has 30 teeth.\nThe dentist drills 4 teeth.\nHe caps 7 more teeth than he drills.\nSo he caps 4 + 7 = 11 teeth.\nThe total number of teeth the dentist fixes is 4 + 11 = 15.\nThe percentage of teeth the dentist fixes is 15 / 30 = 0.5.\nThe answer is 0.5.\n\nAnswer_19:\nThe company sells 4000 gallons of milk at $3.5 per gallon.\nSo the total cost is 4000 * 3.5 = $14000.\n2/5 of the milk is returned.\nSo 2/5 * 4000 = 1600 gallons are returned.\nThe refund is 1600 * 3.5 = $5600.\nThe answer is 5600.\n\nAnswer_20:\nWendy is five times as old as Colin will be seven years from now.\nSo Wendy is 5 * (Colin's age + 7).\nIn 25 years, Colin will be a third as old as Wendy is now.\nSo Colin's age + 25 = 1/3 * Wendy's age.\nWe can solve for Colin's age by substituting Wendy's age in terms of Colin's age.\n5 * (Colin's age + 7) = Colin's age + 25.\n5 * Colin's age + 35 = Colin's age + 25.\n4 * Colin's age = -10.\nColin's age = -10 / 4 = -2.5.\nThe answer is -2.5.\n\nAnswer_21:\nBob spends $27000 on books.\nHe can buy 100 books for $